# Urban-Offline Cline Skills
# Offline-First Emergency Preparedness App
# Vision: Locally AI × Kiwix Hybrid for iOS & Android

## 1. Transformers.js AI Integration

**Expertise Domain:** Browser-based machine learning inference using Hugging Face Transformers.js

**Capabilities:**
- Loading and running ONNX models in browser/WebView environments
- WebGPU acceleration with WebGL fallback strategies
- Text generation with streaming (token-by-token output)
- Model quantization (INT8/INT4) for reduced memory footprint
- Memory management for large language models (500MB-2GB)
- Worker-based inference to avoid blocking UI thread
- Custom ONNX model import and validation

**Key APIs & Patterns:**
```javascript
// Model loading with progress
const engine = await TransformersEngine.getInstance();
await engine.initialize('onnx-community/TinyLlama-1.1B-Chat-v1.0', onProgress);

// Streaming generation
for await (const token of engine.generateStream(prompt, { max_tokens: 512 })) {
  yield token;
}

// Device selection (WebGPU > WebGL > WASM)
const device = await engine._getBestDevice(); // 'webgpu' | 'webgl' | 'cpu'
```

**Apply To:**
- `src/services/ai/TransformersEngine.js` - Core inference engine
- `src/services/ai/AIModelManager.js` - Model lifecycle management
- `src/services/ai/ModelImporter.js` - Custom ONNX import
- `src/services/ai/RAGPipeline.js` - Retrieval-augmented generation

**Troubleshooting:**
- WebGPU not available → Fall back to WebGL → Fall back to WASM
- Out of memory → Unload current model before loading new one
- Model corruption → Validate checksum, re-download if mismatch

---

## 2. Capacitor Native Bridge

**Expertise Domain:** Cross-platform native mobile development with Capacitor

**Capabilities:**
- iOS/Android plugin architecture and native bridge communication
- Native storage: SQLite + Filesystem hybrid approach
- Status bar and navigation customization for immersive UX
- Haptics and vibration patterns for tactile feedback
- App lifecycle management (background/foreground/termination)
- Hardware back button handling (Android)
- Battery monitoring and power-aware features

**Key APIs & Patterns:**
```javascript
// Platform detection
import { isNativeMobile, isIOSNative, isAndroidNative } from './utils/platform';

// Native storage
const { Filesystem, Directory } = await import('@capacitor/filesystem');
await Filesystem.writeFile({
  path: 'models/tinyllama.onnx',
  data: base64Data,
  directory: Directory.Documents
});

// Haptics
import { HapticsService } from './services/HapticsService';
await HapticsService.impact('heavy'); // light | medium | heavy
```

**Apply To:**
- `src/services/storage/NativeStorage.js` - SQLite + Filesystem implementation
- `src/services/HapticsService.js` - Cross-platform haptics
- `src/services/power/BatteryManager.js` - Power monitoring
- `src/App.jsx` - Status bar, back button handling

**Troubleshooting:**
- Plugin not available → Check Capacitor version compatibility
- Permission denied → Add to AndroidManifest.xml / Info.plist
- Storage write fails → Check quota, use Directory.Documents

---

## 3. Offline Storage Architecture

**Expertise Domain:** Client-side data persistence with IndexedDB and SQLite

**Capabilities:**
- IndexedDB schema design with object stores and indexes
- SQLite FTS5 full-text search implementation
- Storage quota management and LRU eviction
- Data migration strategies between schema versions
- Blob storage optimization for large files (models, maps, content)
- Transaction safety and error recovery
- Cross-platform storage abstraction layer

**Key APIs & Patterns:**
```javascript
// Storage abstraction
import { db, initStorage } from './services/db';
await initStorage();
await db.put('models', { id: 'tinyllama', data: modelBlob });

// Web: IndexedDB via idb library
// Native: SQLite + Filesystem hybrid

// Quota handling
try {
  await db.put('content', largeData);
} catch (error) {
  if (error.name === 'QuotaExceededError') {
    // Trigger LRU eviction or show user warning
  }
}
```

**Apply To:**
- `src/services/storage/WebStorage.js` - IndexedDB implementation
- `src/services/storage/NativeStorage.js` - SQLite implementation
- `src/services/db.js` - Storage abstraction entry point
- `src/services/dataManager.js` - Region/content management

**Troubleshooting:**
- Database corruption → Delete and recreate with version bump
- Quota exceeded → Implement LRU eviction for old content
- Slow queries → Add indexes, optimize FTS5 queries

---

## 4. ZIM/Kiwix Content Format

**Expertise Domain:** Offline Wikipedia content distribution and retrieval

**Capabilities:**
- ZIM file structure (header, clusters, directories, URLs)
- XZ compression decompression (WASM implementation)
- Content addressing by URL namespace (A/, I/, M/, etc.)
- Full-text indexing of article content
- Delta update mechanisms for content synchronization
- MIME type detection and content serving
- Embedded image and media extraction

**Key APIs & Patterns:**
```javascript
// ZIM file processing
import { processZimFile } from './scripts/process-zim';
const content = await processZimFile(fileBuffer);

// Content addressing
const article = await zimReader.getArticleByUrl('A/First_aid');
const image = await zimReader.getImageByUrl('I/first_aid_kit.png');

// Search index
const results = await zimReader.search('CPR emergency');
```

**Apply To:**
- `scripts/process-zim.js` - ZIM file processing
- `src/services/contentSync.js` - Content synchronization
- `src/services/DatasetRegistry.js` - Content pack management
- `src/services/ai/RAGPipeline.js` - Content retrieval for AI

**Troubleshooting:**
- ZIM corruption → Validate checksum before import
- Out of memory → Stream content instead of loading entire file
- Search not working → Rebuild FTS index during installation

---

## 5. Emergency UX Design

**Expertise Domain:** Critical-use interface design for high-stress scenarios

**Capabilities:**
- Triage decision tree patterns using Ink.js narrative engine
- Progressive disclosure in time-critical flows
- Accessibility compliance (WCAG 2.1 AA, VoiceOver/TalkBack)
- High-contrast, high-visibility UI design
- Offline-first information architecture
- Cognitive load reduction techniques
- Panic-proof interaction patterns

**Key APIs & Patterns:**
```javascript
// Ink.js integration
import { InkService } from './services/InkService';
const story = await InkService.loadStory('health/cpr.ink.json');
const currentStep = story.continue();
const choices = story.currentChoices;

// Critical content loading
import { SuspenseWrapper } from './components/SuspenseWrapper';
<SuspenseWrapper fallback={<SkeletonPage />}>
  <TriageScreen />
</SuspenseWrapper>

// Error boundaries for resilience
import { ErrorBoundary } from './components/ErrorBoundary';
<ErrorBoundary fallback={<ErrorRecoveryUI />}>
  <CriticalContent />
</ErrorBoundary>
```

**Apply To:**
- `src/components/TriageScreen.jsx` - Interactive decision trees
- `src/components/ProtocolView.jsx` - Emergency protocol display
- `src/services/InkService.js` - Ink.js integration
- `src/components/CriticalContentBanner.jsx` - Missing content warnings

**Design Principles:**
- **Speed over beauty:** Critical content loads in <100ms
- **Reliability over intelligence:** Triage uses deterministic Ink.js, not AI
- **Clarity over density:** Large touch targets, simple language
- **Resilience over features:** Graceful degradation at every level

**Troubleshooting:**
- Content not loading → Show CriticalContentBanner with actionable steps
- AI unavailable → Fall back to keyword search and static content
- User panic → Simplify UI, enlarge touch targets, reduce options

